      "text": "To determine the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles in the new figure, we need to first count the total number of blue and green tiles in the original figure and then adjust for the border added in the new figure.\n\n**Step 1: Count the number of blue tiles in the original figure.**\n\nThe original figure consists of 13 blue tiles. These tiles are arranged in a hexagonal pattern. The pattern of blue tiles in the original figure can be visualized as follows (each grid represents a side of a hexagon):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{ccccccccc}\nB & B & B & B & B \\\\\nB & B & B & B & B \\\\\nB & B & B & B & B \\\\\nB & B & B & B & B \\\\\nB & B & B & B & B \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 13 blue tiles.\n\n**Step 2: Count the number of green tiles in the original figure.**\n\nThe original figure consists of 6 green tiles. These tiles are arranged in a hexagonal pattern. The pattern of green tiles in the original figure can be visualized as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{ccccccccc}\nG & G & G & G & G \\\\\nG & G & G & G & G \\\\\nG & G & G & G & G \\\\\nG & G & G & G & G \\\\\nG & G & G & G & G \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 6 green tiles.\n\n**Step 3: Determine the number of green tiles in the new figure.**\n\nThe new figure is created by adding a border of green tiles around the original figure. The border will consist of a ring of green tiles around the entire figure. The number of green tiles in each row around the border will be the same as the number of green tiles in the inner ring minus 1 (since the tiles at the corners are counted twice).\n\nThe innermost ring has 6 green tiles. The next ring will have 6 green tiles minus 2 (one green tile is at the corner that is double counted), which is 4 green tiles. The next ring will have 4 green tiles minus 2 (one green tile is at the corner that is double counted), which is 2 green tiles. The outermost ring will have 2 green tiles minus 2 (one green tile is at the corner that is double counted), which is 0 green tiles.\n\nSo, the total number of green tiles in the new figure is:\n\\[ 6 + 4 + 2 + 0 = 12 \\]\n\n**Step 4: Determine the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles in the new figure.**\n\nThe original figure had 13 blue tiles and 6 green tiles, so the total number of tiles is:\n\\[ 13 + 6 = 19 \\]\n\nThe new figure has 12 green tiles and \\(13 - 1 = 12\\) blue tiles (since 1 tile is subtracted when counting the new blue tiles), so the total number of tiles in the new figure is:\n\\[ 12 + 12 = 24 \\]\n\nThe difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles in the new figure is:\n\\[ 24 - 12 = 12 \\]\n\nThus, the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles in the new figure is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
