      "text": "Given the initial figure with 13 blue hexagonal tiles and 6 green hexagonal tiles, forming a larger hexagon, we need to determine the effect of adding a border of green tiles with the same shape.\n\nFirst, let's analyze the structure of the original figure. We can observe that the figure has a specific symmetry and regularity. Upon closer inspection, we can see that it is composed of a central hexagon with surrounding layers. The outermost layer of the original figure is composed of green tiles, and we need to determine the number of green tiles in this new border.\n\n### Step-by-Step Breakdown\n\n1. **Original Figure:**\n   - Central hexagon with 13 blue tiles.\n   - Surrounding layers consist of green tiles.\n\n2. **Border Analysis:**\n   - The border consists of a ring of green tiles around the central hexagon and the surrounding layers.\n   - We need to find the number of green tiles in this border.\n\n### Counting the Green Tiles in the Border\n\nTo determine the number of green tiles in the border, we can use a systematic approach:\n- Start by counting the number of tiles in the border.\n- Each ring of the border will have a different pattern of green tiles.\n\nWe can count the number of green tiles in each ring by observing the structure:\n- **Innermost ring:** No green tiles (since the layer is blue).\n- **Second ring:** Each hexagon edge within the blue central hexagon and one additional tile makes a total of \\(6 + 6 = 12\\) green tiles.\n- **Third ring:** Each of the 12 hexagons in the first ring plus the center tile makes a total of \\(12 \\times 1 + 1 = 13\\) green tiles.\n- **Fourth ring:** Same pattern as the third ring but with only one additional hexagon, resulting in \\(13 \\times 1 + 1 = 14\\) green tiles.\n- **Fifth ring:** Same pattern as the fourth ring but with only one additional hexagon, resulting in \\(14 \\times 1 + 1 = 15\\) green tiles.\n- **Sixth ring:** Same pattern as the fifth ring but with only one additional hexagon, resulting in \\(15 \\times 1 + 1 = 16\\) green tiles.\n\n### Summing the Green Tiles in the Border\n\nNow, we sum the number of green tiles in each ring:\n\\[\n0 + 12 + 13 + 14 + 15 + 16 = 72\n\\]\n\n### Total Number of Green Tiles in the New Figure\n\nThe total number of green tiles in the new figure (original plus border) is:\n\\[\n6 \\text{ (original green tiles)} + 72 \\text{ (border green tiles)} = 78\n\\]\n\n### Difference Between Green and Blue Tiles\n\nFinally, we find the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles:\n\\[\n78 - 13 = 65\n\\]\n\nThus, the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles in the new figure is \\(\\boxed{65}\\).",
