      "text": "To determine the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles in the new figure, we start by calculating the number of tiles in the original figure and then add the new border.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the number of tiles in the original figure. The figure forms a hexagon with 13 blue tiles and 6 green tiles:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total tiles in original figure} = 13 + 6 = 19\n\\]\n\nNext, we add the border of green tiles around the original figure. The new figure will add a border of 10 green tiles (5 on each side, but we subtract 2 because the corners are counted twice):\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total tiles in the new figure} = 19 + 10 = 29\n\\]\n\nIn the new figure, the total number of blue tiles remains the same at 13, and the total number of green tiles is the original number plus the new border tiles:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total tiles in the new figure (green)} = 6 + 10 = 16\n\\]\n\nNow, we find the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles in the new figure:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Difference} = 16 - 13 = 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles in the new figure is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
