      "text": "To find the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles in the new figure, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the total number of blue and green tiles after the border is added.\n2. Calculate the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles.\n\nFirst, let's count the tiles in the original figure:\n- There are 13 blue tiles.\n- There are 6 green tiles.\n\nNext, we add the border. The border is made up of green tiles with the same size and shape as the blue tiles, so the number of green tiles is increased by the number of blue tiles in the border.\n\nSince the border forms a repeating pattern every two tiles (which is the same as the blue tile), and there are 3 blue tiles in the border (one tile at the beginning and two tiles at each end of the border), the number of green tiles added is:\n\\[ 3 \\]\n\nSo, the new number of green tiles is:\n\\[ 6 + 3 = 9 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles in the new figure. The new total number of blue tiles is:\n\\[ 13 \\]\n\nThe difference is:\n\\[ 9 - 13 = -4 \\]\n\nTherefore, the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles in the new figure is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-4}\n\\]",
